 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the penal law, in relation to aggravated sexual abuse",
    "basePrintNo": "S6071",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6071-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§130.00, 130.65-a, 130.66, 130.67 & 130.70, Pen L",
    "lawSection": "Penal Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6071\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the penal law, in relation to aggravated sexual abuse\n\n\n PURPOSE :\nTo make the aggravated sexual abuse statutes consistent with the\ncriminal sexual act statutes by adding the word \"anus\" to the list of\ncertain parts of the body of a victim.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nSection 1 through 6 amends the penal law to include the word \"anus\" to\nthe list of certain body parts in for purposes relating to defining\naggravated sexual contact and aggravated sexual abuse in the first,\nsecond, third and fourth degrees.\n\nSection 7 sets the effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThis legislation makes the aggravated sexual abuse statutes consistent\nwith the criminal sexual act statutes. Currently, the word \"rectum\" is\nin the aggravated sexual abuse statutes, whereas \"anus\" is the word\nused in the criminal sexual act statutes. Both statutes criminalize\nsexual assault, yet the inconsistency in the statutes has resulted in\nunintended and inconsistent results.  There is a medical/anatomical\ndifference between the two parts of the body.  In order to prove the\ncommission of the crime of aggravated sexual abuse, victims, including\nchildren, have had to give detailed testimony in court as the depth of\npenetration: the rectum being more internal.  Cases have been\ndismissed and defendants have been found innocent because prosecutors\nhave have not been able to prove that a foreign object or finger was\ninserted during a criminal act, into the rectum because the anus is\nthe place of insertion.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect on the ninetieth day after it shall have\nbecome law.\n",
